StringTable InfoMiningSmelting
{
	Entry _strings
	[
		{
			String _name = "MiningSmelting";
			String _text = "Mining & Smelting";
		}
		{
			String _name = "MiningSmeltingTitle1";
			String _text = "Mining, Assaying & Metallurgy";
		}
		{
			String _name = "MiningSmeltingTitle2";
			String _text = "- of the ores, minerals, stone and raw earth materials -";
		}
		{
			String _name = "MiningSmeltingTitle3";
			String _text = "- and of the fuels & fluxes for metallurgy -";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text01";
			String _text = "Iron, that is, pure native iron, if there is any to be found in the mineral Kingdom, is indeed of the utmost scarcity. It is no longer available as a mined or harvested metal from the surface. Instead Iron Ore is extracted; mostly it is available from mines, but there is also a small, finite amount of the ore that can be found on the surface of the map at the start of a game. This is a realistic change in the process of producing Iron.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text01a";
			String _text = "Mining (and Stone cutting) is characteristically a dangerous occupation in the game, this is now lessened to a certain degree by an extra cost. Mining is expensive with at a minimum, a cost of either a log or piece of timber for every cycle. Deeper, bigger mines may also require lamp oil or candles to operate.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text01b";
			String _text = "Though stone can be taken from the surface by any Laborers with normal tools, quarried stone will now require the use of the specialist utensils for every cycle: 'Tools:Stonemason', a crafted good & utensil, made at blacksmiths. Like with the Miners, Stonecutters now also have a lessened likelihood of occupational death.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02";
			String _text = "Iron Ore needs to be smelted in a very hot furnace to remove impurities and be transformed into the most rigid of metals; Iron.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02a";
			String _text = "Iron Ore";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02b";
			String _text = "Mostly mined, though a small amount is found upon the surface. The ore of iron has no certain form; being altogether irregular, most common of a rusty colour. It is this colour that betrays the amount of Iron it contains and being of the most fusible iron ore.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02c";
			String _text = "Extracted in quantities of 3-5 Iron Ore.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02copper";
			String _text = "Copper Ore also needs a furnace of great heat to be smelted into a solid metallic form of Copper.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02coppera";
			String _text = "Copper Ore";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02copperb";
			String _text = "Mostly mined, though a large amount can be found upon the surface. The ore of copper, sometimes when first mined, is of the darkest red-blue, but before even reaching the surface; oxidises and turns the most beautiful colours of blue and green.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02copperc";
			String _text = "Extracted in cycles of 3-5 Copper Ore.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02tin";
			String _text = "Tin Ore will need a furnace to be smelted into a solid metallic form of Tin, though it is also used along with Copper Ore to forge Bronze.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02tina";
			String _text = "Tin Ore";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02tinb";
			String _text = "Mined, though quantities are found upon the surface. The most rich ore of tin is of a black or dark colour, of a polyhedral, but altogether irregular figure, often its surface is very glossy. Commonly it can be found in alluvial deposits along riverbanks.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02tinc";
			String _text = "Extracted in cycles of 3-5 Tin Ore.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text03";
			String _text = "Silver Ore must also be smelted, but at a slower and lower temperature within a finery furnace to extract the Silver proper.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02silvera";
			String _text = "Silver Ore";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02silverb";
			String _text = "The ore of silver is only mined, and though sometimes it is found in its most purest, native form, to be thought of such value is nought. For it certainly contains sulphur and arsenick. As such all silver from a mine must be smelted along with the not of purest ores.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02silverc";
			String _text = "Extracted in cycles of 3-5 Silver Ore.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text03Gold1";
			String _text = "Gold; of all the other metals it is most frequently found native, free of sulphur and arsenick. There is no ore I know, in which Gold constituted the greatest metallick part. There are indeed several ores sold under that title, but under strict examination, are found not to be such. It has sometimes happened, that many people deceived by the red-yellowish colour of these ores, looking as if there was Gold in them, have mistaken them for gold ores. But, I never saw any body grow rich by means of them, or from what little gold that may be melted out of them.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text04";
			String _text = "To get a blacksmith's furnace or forge hot enough to smelt and extract ores, requires fuels that can burn to a higher temperature, and longer than firewood or coal (both of these have too many impurities, burn irregular and too fast). The use of a Metallurgical fuel is now essential in all elements of metallurgy:";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text05";
			String _text = "Charcoal";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text05a";
			String _text = "A product of logs, Charcoal is made primitively in a charcoal pile, or in a charcoal kiln (coming soon).";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text05b";
			String _text = "Logs are heated with an absence of oxygen, pyrolysis or the charring begins, this removes the impurities and from this, approx. 34-55 Charcoal is produced from every input of 21 Logs.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text06";
			String _text = "Coke";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text06a";
			String _text = "A product of coal, Coke is 'cooked', much like charcoal; primitively in a piled coal hearth (coming soon), where the coal is piled up and covered with earth, or in a beehive shaped coke oven it is produced faster.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text06b";
			String _text = "The process requires 21 mined Coal to produce approx. 21-34 Coke.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text08";
			String _text = "The forging of metals is quick and achieved under very hot conditions, this means there is often much wastage in the amount of ore used over what is finally produced.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text09";
			String _text = "The introduction of a flux into a furnace along with the ore and fuel, allows half the quantity of ore to be used while still maintaining the same output:";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text10";
			String _text = "Lime (a.k.a. Quicklime)";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text10a";
			String _text = "Produced in an oven similar in shape to a coke oven, Lime is the product of softer (higher in calcium) Stone. The stone is piled in an oven where it is heated with a fuel until it reacts and becomes a white-grey powder.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text10b";
			String _text = "A single large piece of Stone with the addition of a fuel is likely to produce approx. 5-8 Lime.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text10c";
			String _text = "The use of Lime in the furnace when smelting metals, reacts with the ores helping separate the impurities. Lime is also used as a building material, acting as a strong binder and also increasing the thermal insulation of a building.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2MadeFrom";
			String _text = "is made from:";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2MadeFromOr";
			String _text = "or:";
		}
		{
			String _name = "valueTip";
			String _text = "Value of product";
		}
		{
			String _name = "valueTolTip";
			String _text = "Value of product, this product has a fluctuating value; as such traders may offer or buy at a price within this range";
		}
		{
			String _name = "weightTip";
			String _text = "Weight of product";
		}
		{
			String _name = "quantityTip";
			String _text = "Quantity of product produced by educated-or-uneducated workers";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text01";
			String _text = "Iron";
		}
		{
			String _name = "Iron00Tip";
			String _text = "The most common and used of all the metals; Iron has its own limit to control production. Used importantly as a material to produce Tools, it is also used in building construction.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text02";
			String _text = "5 Iron Ore + ";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text03";
			String _text = "2 Coke or Charcoal";
		}
		{
			String _name = "Iron01Tip";
			String _text = "This method has a per cycle input cost of 34-36(Charcoal-Coke). Uneducated will make a loss of 2 with coke, or break even with charcoal, for only 1 piece of Iron will be made, meanwhile; an Educated worker will make a total profit of 32-34 (Coke-Charcoal) or 16-17 per piece of Iron.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text04";
			String _text = "3 Iron Ore + ";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text05";
			String _text = "1 Lime + ";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text06";
			String _text = "2 Coke or Charcoal";
		}
		{
			String _name = "Iron02Tip";
			String _text = "This method has a per cycle input cost of 31-33(Charcoal-Coke). Uneducated will make a profit of 1-3(Coke-Charcoal) for only 1 piece of Iron will be made, meanwhile; an Educated worker will make a total profit of 35-37 or 17.5-18.5 per piece of Iron. As Coke is to Charcoal, Lime is potentially a cheaper material to produce than Iron Ore, the total end-to-end profits are likely more.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "IronQty";
			String _text = "Output: 1-2";
		}
		{
			String _name = "IronValue";
			String _text = "34";
		}
		{
			String _name = "IronWeight";
			String _text = "25";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text01c";
			String _text = "Copper";
		}
		{
			String _name = "Copper00Tip";
			String _text = "Copper is produced under the limit of Metals, Alloys & forged to control production. Uses are mostly in building construction, though it can also be used to make Tools and other copper-wares.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text02c";
			String _text = "5 Copper Ore + ";
		}
		{
			String _name = "Copper01Tip";
			String _text = "This method has a per cycle input cost of 34-36(Charcoal-Coke). Uneducated will make a loss of 4-6 for only 1 piece of Copper will be made, meanwhile; an Educated worker will make a total profit of 24-26 (Coke-Charcoal) or 12-13 per piece of Copper.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text04c";
			String _text = "3 Copper Ore + ";
		}
		{
			String _name = "Copper02Tip";
			String _text = "This method has a per cycle input cost of 31-33(Charcoal-Coke). Uneducated will make a loss of 1-3 for only 1 piece of Copper will be made, meanwhile; an Educated worker will make a total profit of 27-29 (Coke-Charcoal)or 13.5-14.5 per piece of Copper. As Coke is to Charcoal, Lime is potentially a cheaper material to produce than Copper Ore, the total end-to-end profits are likely more.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "CopperQty";
			String _text = "Output: 1-2";
		}
		{
			String _name = "CopperValue";
			String _text = "30";
		}
		{
			String _name = "CopperWeight";
			String _text = "25";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text01cTin";
			String _text = "Tin";
		}
		{
			String _name = "Tin00Tip";
			String _text = "Tin is produced under the limit of Metals, Alloys & forged to control production. Uses are in making Tinware and being a valuable good in trade.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text02cTin";
			String _text = "5 Tin Ore + ";
		}
		{
			String _name = "Tin01Tip";
			String _text = "This method has a per cycle input cost of 39-41(Charcoal-Coke). Uneducated will make a loss of 3-5 for only 1 piece of Tin will be made, meanwhile; an Educated worker will make a total profit of 31-33 (Coke-Charcoal) or 15.5-16.5 per piece of Tin.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text04cTin";
			String _text = "3 Tin Ore + ";
		}
		{
			String _name = "Tin02Tip";
			String _text = "This method has a per cycle input cost of 34-36(Charcoal-Coke). Uneducated will break even with coke, or make a profit 2 with charcoal, meanwhile; an Educated worker will make a total profit of 36-38 (Coke-Charcoal)or 18-19 per piece of Tin. As Coke is to Charcoal, Lime is potentially a cheaper material to produce than Tin Ore, the total end-to-end profits are likely more.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "TinQty";
			String _text = "Output: 1-2";
		}
		{
