StringTable InfoPotteryGlass
{
	Entry _strings
	[
		{
			String _name = "PotteryGlass";
			String _text = "Pottery & Glass";
		}
		{
			String _name = "PotteryGlassTitle1";
			String _text = "Pottery, Bricks, Tiles & Glass-making";
		}
		{
			String _name = "PotteryGlassTitle2";
			String _text = "- of the raw earth materials, as vessels and crown glass -";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text01";
			String _text = "Pottery is an important crafted good & utensil, used in everyday life by citizens. As many different objects: a simple lamp, it is used as an essential construction item (particularly in mines), and as vessels for the mixing and storage and preserving of items.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text02";
			String _text = "There is no denying the importance of the use of Bricks and Roof-tiles in building construction. In most cases they are lighter and more durable than their stone, wood and thatch counterparts. And when used in residence building construction, they will increase and give better warmth and heat retention.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text03";
			String _text = "Glass is a marvellous creation; crown Glass, that of the kind used for windows in buildings, has many benefits: by letting in more light, it allows homes to use less fuel, as no longer are we living in dark, dank stone hovels. Useful in production buildings, more light allows work to be achieved faster and of better quality.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text04";
			String _text = "Glassware, like pottery is made and used as vessels for the mixing and storage of items, it is also used by a Finery to produce Amulets.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column1text05";
			String _text = "Further showing the incredible uses of the material: Lime; it can also be used in the production of pottery & glass. In the production of Pottery, it along with Sand, takes the place of clay in the recipe. In the production of glass, it acts in a much similar way in being a binder for a stronger glass, but it also allows for less use of Sand.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2AreMadeFrom";
			String _text = "are made from:";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2MadeFrom";
			String _text = "is made from:";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2MadeFromOr";
			String _text = "or:";
		}
		{
			String _name = "valueTip";
			String _text = "Value of product";
		}
		{
			String _name = "valueTolTip";
			String _text = "Value of product, this product has a fluctuating value; as such traders may offer or buy at a price within this range";
		}
		{
			String _name = "weightTip";
			String _text = "Weight of product";
		}
		{
			String _name = "quantityTip";
			String _text = "Quantity of product produced by educated-or-uneducated workers";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text01";
			String _text = "Pottery";
		}
		{
			String _name = "Pottery00Tip";
			String _text = "A widely used crafted good, Pottery offers many functions for citizens in production and construction. Uses the Crafted Goods & Utensils limit to control production.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text02";
			String _text = "4 Clay + ";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text03";
			String _text = "1 Coke or Charcoal";
		}
		{
			String _name = "Pottery01Tip";
			String _text = "This method has a per cycle input cost of 19-20(Charcoal-Coke). Uneducated will make a total profit of 4-5 (Coke-Charcoal) for only 3 pieces of Pottery will be made, meanwhile; an Educated worker will make 4 pieces of Pottery with a total profit of 12-13 or 3-3.25 per piece of Pottery.";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text04";
			String _text = "2 Sand + ";
		}
		{
			String _name = "column2text05";
			String _text = "1 Lime + ";
		}
		{
